RECOVERY

Check stops bad step before run. Nothing ran. Code kept in `rejected`. Fix by
edit, not rewrite: edit forms change rejected, then fixed code checked and run
as this step.
- (revise :old "text" :new "text") replace text found once in rejected. No
  match or many fails: quote more around it.
- (rename old new) rename symbol everywhere in rejected. Strings untouched.
- (close-parens) close parens left open, at end.
- (add-arg f :key value) add keyword arg to the one call of f.
- (push-arg f value) add positional arg to the one call of f, before its
  keywords.
Edit forms go alone in step, applied in order. Rewrite only when no edit says
it.
